Autoplay script:
```
if (window.__auto) clearInterval(window.__auto);
window.__auto = setInterval(()=>{
 const g=window.__cryout;
 if(!g || g.state!=='playing') return;
 const t=g.audio.time;
 for(const n of g.notes){
   if(n.state==='pending' && t>=n.data.t-0.02 && t<=n.data.t+0.09){
     g.pressLane(n.lane);
     if(n.type==='hold'){ setTimeout(()=>g.releaseLane(n.lane), Math.max(0,(n.endTime - g.audio.time))*1000); }
   }
 }
}, 12);
```
But pressLane might hit wrong note if multiple same lane; fine.
For holds, release via setTimeout based on audio time, but if paused? testing no pause. For hold, press at head; `holdNote` set; release after duration. But pressing same lane for next note while holding? chart avoids. Good.
Need ensure each note pressed once: it becomes holding/done, so no duplicate.
For hold auto release, setTimeout sufficient.
Call `pressLane` not keydown so pads won't light; for screenshot of gameplay effects, that's fine but pads won't show presses. Could dispatch keydown/keyup instead to simulate input and pad visuals. Use `document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown',{code:...}))` and keyup. But global handler uses `held` and calls press. That also lights pads. For autoplay, use actual events and schedule keyup. keyup release holds. Let's map lane codes.
```
const codes=['KeyA','KeyS','KeyD','KeyF','KeyJ','KeyK','KeyL','Semicolon'];
function down(lane){ if(held check?) dispatch keydown (repeat false) }
```
But game's held prevents duplicate; after tap, key remains held until keyup shortly. If we keyup after 40ms, fine. For holds, keyup at end. This will animate pads. Use direct pressLane plus pad classes? Better events.

Script:
```
clearInterval(window.__auto);
const codes=[...];
window.__auto = setInterval(()=>{
 const g=window.__cryout; if(!g||g.state!=='playing') return;
 const t=g.audio.time;
 for(const n of g.notes){
  if(n.state==='pending' && t>=n.data.t-0.015 && t<=n.data.t+0.075){
    document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keydown',{code:codes[n.lane]}));
    if(n.type==='hold'){
      setTimeout(()=>document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup',{code:codes[n.lane]})), Math.max(30,(n.endTime-g.audio.time)*1000+60));
    } else {
      setTimeout(()=>document.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent('keyup',{code:codes[n.lane]})), 45);
    }
  }
 }
}, 10);
```
Problem: `n.state` becomes holding but loop next ticks might press again? condition pending only. Good.
- For tapping, keydown event fired; `held[lane]` becomes true; keyup after 45ms. If next note in same lane within 45ms (rare, 16th 150ms), fine.
- For hold, key stays until end.

Then screenshot at ~30s/90s. Use wait. Let's reload and install, then wait 30 sec and screenshot. But we already patched; dev server HMR will reload? Vite HMR may have updated. Use reload.

