content.text:
Portrait results screen has a layout bug: the `.btnrow` items are stacked vertically (RETRY full width, MENU below) and the result panel extends beyond viewport (scroll). The retry/menu layout should be side by side compactly. Also the FC badge absent (fine). The overlay scrolls; acceptable but the buttons look odd.

Also "MAX COMBO 90" with 241 misses makes sense from teleport.

The portrait results page: huge spacing; content fits till y=845 with menu cut? The screenshot height 844; menu at y~800-844, cut at bottom. There's a scrollbar. Since overflow:auto, user can scroll. But better to compact for portrait/small width.

Let's improve `.result-foot` / `.btnrow` on narrow screens:

Currently `.btnrow` probably display flex with gap and wrap. On 620px media, `.cta{width:100%;min-width:0}` makes RETRY full width; MENU is a ghost button maybe also width? The result-foot is flex column? In screenshot, RETRY is a bar spanning ~265px and MENU below-left. Need to make them two equal buttons in a row.

Add in @media (max-width:620px):
```css
.result-foot{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;gap:14px}
.result-foot .btnrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}
.result-foot .btnrow .cta, .result-foot .btnrow .ghost{width:100%;min-width:0}
.result-stats .bigstat b{font-size:...}
.results{padding:20px}
```
But pause modal also uses .btnrow with 3 buttons (resume/restart/quit) — on mobile they'd fill width stacked by `.cta{width:100%}`? Let's check current pause portrait. The pause modal might similarly look off. Let me inspect screenshot pause.jpg (desktop) and maybe test portrait pause later.

