Now lane loop replacing old opacity logic. Need to be careful with spread: old used `(i-3.5)*state.spacing*v.spread`; now use v.spacing. Also ghost logic. Let's write:

```js
for (let i=0;i<8;i++){
 const l=lanes[i];
 const x=(i-3.5)*v.spacing*v.spread;
 ...
 const live = state.active.has(i);
 let ghostAmp=0, bounceAmp=0;
 if (l.ghostFx) {
   const g=l.ghostFx;
   g.t+=dt;
   const p=g.t/g.dur;
   if (p>=1){ l.ghostFx=null; l.ghost.visible=false; l.ghost.material.opacity=0; }
   else {
     ghostAmp=Math.sin(Math.PI*p);
     if (g.type==='sweep'){
       l.ghost.visible=true;
       l.ghost.position.set(0,0.25+p*10.5,0.08);
       const s=0.62+0.5*ghostAmp;
       l.ghost.scale.set(s,s,1);
       l.ghost.material.opacity=ghostAmp*0.95;
       l.ghost.material.color.copy(l.targetColor).lerp(white,0.35+ghostAmp*0.4);
     } else { bounceAmp=ghostAmp; l.ghost.visible=false; }
   }
 }
 const vis = live?1:0;
 const lineTarget = live ? (i%2?0.86:0.96)*0.58 : ghostAmp*0.5;
 ...
 l.line.material.opacity += (lineTarget - ...)
 beamTarget = live ? 0.065+pulse*0.03 : ghostAmp*0.05
 ringTarget = live?0.95 : (l.ghostFx?.type==='bounce'?ghostAmp*0.9:ghostAmp*0.22)
 glowTarget = live?0.14+flash*0.3 : ghostAmp*0.12 + ...
```
Careful: l.ghostFx may be null after update; use `bounceAmp` for ring.

Also l.flash decay; inactive lane flash from ghostBounce. Color.

Ring scale: `v.ring * (1 + pulse*0.045*(0.4+energy) + l.flash*0.22 + bounceAmp*0.55)`.

For inactive rings, if sweep, show faint ring briefly? ringTarget ghostAmp*0.22 perhaps. Fine.

Need `l.ghost` object exists. Let's edit.

