content.text:
Now replace worldPoint/laneScreen functions. Use cached matrix and geometry. Also add setTempo. Let's replace block.

```
const screenV = new THREE.Vector3();
const screenV2 = new THREE.Vector3();
function worldPoint(lane,y){ const v=new Vector3(0,y,0.2); return lanes[lane].group.localToWorld(v);}
function updateLaneScreen(){
  camera.updateMatrixWorld();
  // update parent stage matrix then lane groups
  stage.updateMatrixWorld(true); // can be expensive but only lanes/notes
  ...
}
```
Optimization: `stage.updateMatrixWorld(true)` updates all descendants (all notes). Could use `laneRoot.updateMatrixWorld(true)`? laneRoot parent stage; stage matrix updated by renderer each frame. Calling `stage.updateWorldMatrix(true,false)` updates stage's ancestors (scene) but not children; then for each lane `lane.group.updateWorldMatrix(false,true)` updates lane subtree (notes too). That's still all notes. Instead to project ring/top, we need lane group world matrix only, not notes. `lane.group.updateWorldMatrix(true,false)` updates ancestors and lane group but not children; the lane group's children (ring etc) not needed for ring position? The ring's local position (0,0.02,0.22) is what we project; we can use lane group's matrix and local points manually:
```
lane.group.updateWorldMatrix(true,false);
const m = lane.group.matrixWorld;
screenV.set(0, 0.04, 0.22).applyMatrix4(m)
```
`updateWorldMatrix(true,false)` updates parents and self; good. For 8 lanes, cheap. Then camera.updateMatrixWorld(). Project. Cache.
- But notes positions use lane group's matrix; renderer updates them; fine.
- `laneScreenGeometry` returns cached l.screen if computed this frame; call update in animate end.
- Need ensure stage transform update before projecting. `stage.updateWorldMatrix(true,false)` then each lane group update. `updateWorldMatrix(true,false)` on each lane will update its parent (laneRoot/stage) repeatedly, but cheap. Could first `stage.updateWorldMatrix(true,false)`, then `lane.group.updateWorldMatrix(false,false)` to only self using parent matrix. Use that.

Add `updateLaneScreen()`:
```
const ring = screenV.set(0,0.04,0.22).applyMatrix4(l.group.matrixWorld).project(camera)
const top = screenV2.set(0,11.2,0.22).applyMatrix4(...).project(camera)
const x=..., y=..., topX=..., topY=...
const angle = Math.atan2(topX-x, y-topY)
l.screenAngle=angle; l.screen={x,y,topX,topY,angle}
```
Need camera.project? `Vector3.project(camera)` uses camera.matrixWorldInverse & projectionMatrix. Update camera.matrixWorld and matrixWorldInverse? `camera.updateMatrixWorld()` updates. Fine.
- Top y 11.8; if beyond screen, pads height might huge. Use 11.5. We'll use for pad.
- `laneScreenPoints` returns cache after update.
- In initial layout before animate, cache may be null. `laneScreenGeometry(i)` calls update if null.
- `laneScreenXs`.
- `laneScreenAngle(i)`.

Let's edit.

input.newString:
function laneX(i) { return lanes[i].baseX; }
function laneZ(i) { return ARC * lanes[i].baseX * lanes[i].baseX; }

function worldPoint(lane, y) {
  return lanes[lane].group.localToWorld(new THREE.Vector3(0, y, 0.2));
}

const screenV = new THREE.Vector3();
const screenV2 = new THREE.Vector3();
function updateLaneScreen() {
  camera.updateMatrixWorld();
  stage.updateWorldMatrix(true, false);
  for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    const l = lanes[i];
    l.group.updateWorldMatrix(false, false);
    const m = l.group.matrixWorld;
    screenV.set(0, 0.04, 0.22).applyMatrix4(m).project(camera);
    screenV2.set(0, 11.4, 0.22).applyMatrix4(m).project(camera);
    const x = (screenV.x * 0.5 + 0.5) * innerWidth;
    const y = (-screenV.y * 0.5 + 0.5) * innerHeight;
    const topX = (screenV2.x * 0.5 + 0.5) * innerWidth;
    const topY = (-screenV2.y * 0.5 + 0.5) * innerHeight;
    l.screenAngle = Math.atan2(topX - x, y - topY);
    l.screen = { x, y, topX, topY, angle: l.screenAngle };
  }
}

function laneScreenGeometry(i) {
  if (!lanes[i].screen) updateLaneScreen();
  return lanes[i].screen;
}

function laneScreenPoints() {
  updateLaneScreen();
  return lanes.map((l) => l.screen);
}

function laneScreenXs() {
  return laneScreenPoints().map((p) => p.x);
}

function laneScreenAngle(i) {
  if (!lanes[i].screen) updateLaneScreen();
  return lanes[i].screenAngle;
}

function setTempo(bpm, offset = 0) {
  state.bpm = bpm || 100;
  state.beatOffset = offset;
}

