content.text:
Now add responsive overrides at end for new UI. Also adjust existing `.results` mobile rules conflict: earlier media at max-width 620 sets `.results{padding:20px}` and `.results h2{font-size:44px...}`; those come before our new block? Our new block inserted before `#toast` (line ~371), which is before responsive section at line ~386. So the old media query rules come after and will override our new base rules at those widths — that's okay for padding/h2, but `.results` width etc from new base still applies. However `.result-stats` rules are irrelevant. But our new `.results h2` selector is `.result-title h2` so `.results h2` media rule applies too (more specific? `.results h2` specificity 0,1,1 vs `.result-title h2` 0,1,1 equal, later wins → media sets 44px on mobile, fine).

`#rank` media sets 80px, fine. Need mobile layout for result-hero: currently 3 columns; on small screens may be cramped. Add new media at end:

```css
@media (max-width:820px){
  .result-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:14px}
  .hero-combo{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;text-align:left}
  .hero-combo span{margin:0}
  .fc{margin-top:0}
  .result-body{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}
  .combo-panel svg{height:82px}
  .rank-wrap{min-width:120px;min-height:110px}
  .rank-orbit{width:118px;height:118px;right:8px}
  #rank{font-size:74px}
  .result-head{gap:8px}
  .compile{grid-template-columns:1fr;justify-items:center;text-align:center;gap:18px}
  .compile-copy .eyebrow{justify-content:center}
  .compile-copy h2{font-size:38px}
  .compile-orbit{width:120px}
  .compile-bars{bottom:-34px}
}
@media (max-width:620px){
  .results{padding:16px}
  .result-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;padding:12px 0;margin:12px 0}
  .hero-score b{font-size:30px}
  .acc-ring{width:88px;height:88px}
  .acc-ring b{font-size:16px}
  .acc-ring small{font-size:6px}
  .result-title h2{font-size:40px}
  .result-meta{font-size:7px;gap:6px}
  .judge-row{grid-template-columns:50px 1fr 30px;font-size:7px}
  .judge-list{gap:6px}
  .combo-panel svg{height:66px}
  .result-foot{margin-top:12px;padding-top:12px}
  .result-footline{width:100%;font-size:7px}
  .result-foot .btnrow{width:100%;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
  .result-foot .btnrow .cta,.result-foot .btnrow .ghost{width:100%;min-width:0}
  .track-card{grid-template-columns:26px 1fr;gap:9px}
  .tc-tags{grid-column:2;justify-content:flex-start;margin-top:2px}
  .track-picker{margin-bottom:12px}
}
@media (max-height:700px){
  .results{padding:14px 18px}
  .result-hero{padding:10px 0;margin:10px 0}
  .result-head .result-title h2{font-size:36px;margin:6px 0 3px}
  .result-title .modal-sub{margin-top:6px}
  .combo-panel svg{height:64px}
  .judge-list{gap:5px}
  .result-foot{margin-top:10px;padding-top:10px}
  #rank{font-size:64px}
  .rank-orbit{width:104px;height:104px}
}
```

Maybe also hide `.result-meta` on very short.

Now, concern: `#resultLoading` overlay has `.overlay` background and uses `display:flex`; `.transition` override good. The result screen is shown via class `show`, but there's `compile` animation.

Also loading progress: user asked "cool animation loading screen after gameplay heading to results". We have the compile transition + rank reveal. Good.

Now also `showResults` currently does `dom.resultLoading.classList.remove('show')` via setTimeout after result shown; result is shown first then loading removed. Actually `showResults` adds result show and then timeout removes loading 60ms later. Fine—crossfade.

Wait finishGame sets loading show, then after progress completes calls showResults. showResults sets result to show and schedules loading removal. Good.

Now the city background: scene.setCity per section. Need intro "moving background city". world chart INTRO city 1, others low. Good. City appears on start menu for selected world? applyTrackUI/selectTrack sets section and city. Yes.

Now also need `#hudTrack` etc exists.

Need to verify scene.js syntax: I added `state.live` etc. Check full scene around lane loop to ensure no leftover references to removed `live` variable conflict. Let me view 940-1120.

